WEBVTT

00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:13.060
We'll find clues on Iliaster here.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:18.630
Yes, and also on who killed my father.

00:00:20.400 --> 00:00:23.470
I know Moment Express.

00:00:23.470 --> 00:00:24.960
What kind of company is it?

00:00:25.200 --> 00:00:29.350
Tell us.  It's our best lead on Iliaster.

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:35.030
Moment Express, also known as ME, is a 
private Moment manufacturing company.

00:00:35.190 --> 00:00:38.950
Our company outsources engine 
manufacturing to them.

00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.650
The Moment built into 
D-Wheels are miniaturized...

00:00:43.650 --> 00:00:49.920
...but the original Moment is a large particle 
accelerator that's tens of kilometers in diameter.

00:00:50.410 --> 00:00:56.830
ME receives funds from around the world 
to use the accelerator to develop Moment.

00:00:56.830 --> 00:00:58.920
It's big business.

00:00:59.220 --> 00:01:02.510
However, the full scope is 
wrapped in mystery.  Some

00:01:02.510 --> 00:01:05.580
say that they're also involved 
in outer space development.

00:01:06.010 --> 00:01:09.150
Just hearing that makes me suspicious.

00:01:09.550 --> 00:01:11.880
Can we investigate their facility?

00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:15.260
It's not easy to get near that company.

00:01:16.050 --> 00:01:17.010
I know!

00:01:17.020 --> 00:01:20.930
My staff is going there 
to test our new engine.

00:01:20.930 --> 00:01:23.630
If you disguise yourself as part 
of the staff, you can sneak in.

00:01:23.810 --> 00:01:24.860
Really?

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:27.610
But if we do that, you might get in trouble.

00:01:27.780 --> 00:01:34.140
I don't mind.  I feel bad about what 
happened during the WRGP preliminaries.

00:01:34.300 --> 00:01:37.840
If we can discover the 
truth, I'm glad to help.

00:01:37.840 --> 00:01:41.090
But make sure you report 
back on the test results.

00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:43.040
Thank you, Rick.

00:01:45.760 --> 00:01:47.330
Riding Duels.

00:01:47.590 --> 00:01:50.460
These duels evolved in the world of speed.

00:01:50.710 --> 00:01:57.270
The people with the legendary marks who 
risked their lives were known as 5D's.

00:02:12.380 --> 00:02:18.550
Reach out your hand and 
grab a bright tomorrow

00:02:18.780 --> 00:02:28.660
Soar in the infinite skies  BELIEVE IN NEXUS

00:02:29.290 --> 00:02:34.900
No one can stop my wild impulses

00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:40.870
My hand sweats as the battle 
intensifies  This Heart Beat

00:02:41.410 --> 00:02:46.640
I can't avoid this fearsome battle

00:02:46.880 --> 00:02:52.250
I don't want it to end here  Go For It!!

00:02:53.350 --> 00:02:58.620
Stand up  Don't tremble in fear alone

00:02:58.790 --> 00:03:04.430
Remember that you have 
friends waiting for you

00:03:04.660 --> 00:03:10.740
I'm not scared and I'll never give 
up, no matter how powerful the enemy

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:17.040
With real courage, I'll never lose

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:46.670
Moment Express Development Organization

00:03:47.160 --> 00:03:50.700
Are you from Bolger & Company?

00:03:52.100 --> 00:03:54.650
I was waiting for you, Mister…

00:03:54.650 --> 00:03:55.650
Daniel.

00:03:55.740 --> 00:03:56.560
Timothy.

00:03:56.800 --> 00:03:57.880
Eva.

00:03:58.280 --> 00:04:00.910
I'm Clark, the person in charge.

00:04:01.700 --> 00:04:04.800
It's sad about what happened to Mr. Bolger.

00:04:04.970 --> 00:04:07.750
However, your company still has many friends.

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:11.970
It proves that he always worked 
hard in building D-Wheels.

00:04:12.530 --> 00:04:14.130
Thank you for those kind words.

00:04:14.130 --> 00:04:17.100
Have we met before?

00:04:17.100 --> 00:04:19.400
No, I don't think so.

00:04:19.400 --> 00:04:21.740
I see.  I'm sorry.

00:04:22.000 --> 00:04:23.230
The course is this way.

00:04:24.260 --> 00:04:25.780
You've met him before?

00:04:26.180 --> 00:04:27.270
Maybe.

00:04:42.110 --> 00:04:44.950
This often happens when Infinity is active.

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:48.040
Infinity?

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:02.370
That's Infinity.

00:05:02.610 --> 00:05:04.120
It's humongous.

00:05:04.610 --> 00:05:06.380
What does this machine do?

00:05:06.880 --> 00:05:11.590
Infinity is our company's experimental 
matter transfer device.

00:05:11.870 --> 00:05:14.030
We accelerate planetary 
particles to high speed inside

00:05:14.030 --> 00:05:16.630
the machine and send them through 
a dimensional distortion.

00:05:16.630 --> 00:05:20.870
In other words, we create a 
wormhole to transfer matter.

00:05:21.390 --> 00:05:25.830
If this becomes practical, we won't need 
to fire rockets into space anymore.

00:05:28.630 --> 00:05:31.870
What is it, Mr. Daniel?

00:05:32.170 --> 00:05:34.080
It's nothing.

00:05:50.590 --> 00:05:54.390
Leave the test run results to me.  You have 
to successfully break in during this time.

00:05:54.620 --> 00:05:58.340
There's no way that they would think that 
they're being hacked from the inside.

00:05:58.860 --> 00:06:01.980
I'll find out what this 
company is really doing.

00:06:03.640 --> 00:06:07.290
I can't believe they invaded 
our enemy's home base.

00:06:07.660 --> 00:06:10.510
I don't know if they're fearless or reckless.

00:06:11.020 --> 00:06:13.620
If there's a connection 
between ME and Iliaster...

00:06:13.620 --> 00:06:15.950
If they discover Yusei's true identity…

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:20.990
I'm having a bad hair day.  I 
have a bad feeling about this.

00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:26.430
Comparing your hair with 
Yusei's destiny is stupid.

00:06:26.430 --> 00:06:27.300
Huh?

00:06:27.580 --> 00:06:29.690
My earring fell out.

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:31.600
Stupid.

00:06:33.590 --> 00:06:34.910
The vase!

00:06:35.430 --> 00:06:37.150
It's okay, Ruka.

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:39.170
Stupid.

00:06:41.300 --> 00:06:42.550
Hot!

00:06:42.570 --> 00:06:45.380
Hot hot hot!

00:06:45.680 --> 00:06:47.470
More bad omens...

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:53.380
There was no information regarding Iliaster.

00:06:53.650 --> 00:06:58.530
But since this company contacted the 
Directors, there must be something.

00:06:58.720 --> 00:07:02.930
We don't have much time until 
the afternoon driving tests.

00:07:02.930 --> 00:07:06.140
The only thing we haven't 
examined is Infinity.

00:07:06.860 --> 00:07:08.750
There might be something there.

00:07:08.740 --> 00:07:13.470
But information regarding 
Infinity is heavily guarded.

00:07:16.250 --> 00:07:18.950
The most important information 
must be behind that door.

00:07:18.950 --> 00:07:22.630
But only special staff can enter there.

00:07:23.150 --> 00:07:29.440
Even if we manage to break in, we'll need a 
specific access key to unlock its biggest secrets.

00:07:30.220 --> 00:07:31.470
Access key?

00:07:32.270 --> 00:07:34.150
Do you know the chief's schedule?

00:07:34.510 --> 00:07:38.410
I knew you were going to ask that!  
He's having lunch with his staff.

00:07:39.050 --> 00:07:41.130
That means his office is empty right now.

00:07:41.720 --> 00:07:42.520
Let's hurry!

00:07:50.290 --> 00:07:51.290
Over there.

00:07:56.840 --> 00:07:57.980
Where's the card key?

00:08:06.610 --> 00:08:07.850
Here it is, Yusei!

00:08:09.290 --> 00:08:10.320
All right, let's go!

00:08:11.860 --> 00:08:12.960
No, wait!

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:17.810
He's coming back!

00:08:28.360 --> 00:08:30.880
I was waiting for you, Chief Clark.

00:08:31.150 --> 00:08:34.370
You're Daniel.  What are you doing here?

00:08:34.540 --> 00:08:38.050
I was waiting for you so 
that I could duel you.

00:08:38.960 --> 00:08:40.300
Duel me?

00:08:40.620 --> 00:08:44.550
Because Rick always brags 
about your dueling skills.

00:08:45.170 --> 00:08:47.180
That's a nice story.

00:08:51.010 --> 00:08:56.250
Stall for time, Yusei.  If he finds out that 
his card key is missing, it's all over.

00:08:57.550 --> 00:09:02.510
Fine.  You want to battle that 
badly, and I'm a duelist.

00:09:02.780 --> 00:09:05.150
But there's a condition.

00:09:05.380 --> 00:09:08.650
We'll battle using special rules.

00:09:08.800 --> 00:09:10.140
Special rules?

00:09:12.560 --> 00:09:15.310
I call it the Concentration Duel!

00:09:15.880 --> 00:09:17.790
Concentration Duel?

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:26.640
What's a Concentration Duel?

00:09:26.960 --> 00:09:29.810
The rules are basically 
the same as a normal duel.

00:09:29.810 --> 00:09:32.340
You declare your action, and 
then you flip over a card.

00:09:32.960 --> 00:09:37.190
For example, if you're going to summon a 
monster, you say that out loud and flip over a card.

00:09:37.900 --> 00:09:40.930
If that card is a monster that fulfills the

00:09:40.930 --> 00:09:43.970
requirements, it's successfully 
summoned.  If not, you put it back.

00:09:44.460 --> 00:09:46.530
It's the same for spells and traps.

00:09:46.530 --> 00:09:51.010
If it fulfills the requirements, then it 
successfully activates.  If not, you put it back.

00:09:51.270 --> 00:09:56.270
But for spells and traps, you can 
only flip over one of each per turn.

00:09:56.270 --> 00:10:01.160
Since all the cards on the table are facedown, 
without that rule, you can flip over all the cards.

00:10:01.920 --> 00:10:04.150
The rules seem simple, but...

00:10:04.540 --> 00:10:09.820
There's one more condition.  
The winner gets all the cards.

00:10:09.820 --> 00:10:10.800
What?

00:10:10.980 --> 00:10:14.570
In other words, the winner 
gets the opponent's deck.

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:17.260
If you accept this condition, 
I'll accept the duel.

00:10:17.860 --> 00:10:23.220
If I lose, I lose my deck.  But I need 
to give Sherry and Bruno more time.

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:26.930
I understand.  We'll play 
under those conditions.

00:10:27.980 --> 00:10:28.770
Fine.

00:10:29.270 --> 00:10:30.360
Duel!

00:10:31.890 --> 00:10:38.350
You can go first.  Since you're not used to 
these rules, I'll give you the advantage.

00:10:38.930 --> 00:10:40.330
Then it's my turn!

00:10:40.800 --> 00:10:42.320
First, I summon a monster.

00:10:44.630 --> 00:10:48.900
The odds of drawing a monster 
from my deck is about 50%.

00:10:49.350 --> 00:10:50.980
I select this card.

00:10:52.250 --> 00:10:58.060
Too bad, but it's not a monster.  
Please put the card back.

00:10:58.580 --> 00:11:02.880
I see.  Under these rules, I 
don't know which card is where.

00:11:03.340 --> 00:11:04.610
Even though this may be pointless…

00:11:05.390 --> 00:11:07.320
I activate a spell card!

00:11:08.870 --> 00:11:11.730
You managed to draw a spell card.

00:11:11.720 --> 00:11:15.150
However, Release Restraint Wave 
requires you to destroy one

00:11:15.150 --> 00:11:19.130
of your Equip Spells to destroy 
all my set spell and trap cards.

00:11:19.500 --> 00:11:23.270
You didn't fulfill its activation 
requirements.  You have to put it back.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:27.000
I activate a trap card.

00:11:30.140 --> 00:11:31.560
I end my turn.

00:11:31.990 --> 00:11:35.140
Even though he knew it would be pointless, 
he still activated a spell and a trap.

00:11:35.370 --> 00:11:38.640
He's starting to get a hang of the rules.

00:11:39.580 --> 00:11:44.100
My turn.  I summon a monster.  I select…

00:11:45.310 --> 00:11:49.450
What?  Under these rules, if you 
activate a spell or trap card

00:11:49.450 --> 00:11:54.580
before summoning a monster, your 
odds of success increase.  So why?

00:11:55.120 --> 00:11:57.060
I select this card.

00:11:59.530 --> 00:12:02.640
Whoa!  I luckily drew a monster.

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:06.500
Hexa Knight is a Level 6 monster, 
but when there are no monsters

00:12:06.500 --> 00:12:10.500
on your field, I can summon it 
without releasing another monster.

00:12:15.110 --> 00:12:20.310
Since you didn't draw a 
monster, I'm now in luck.

00:12:20.670 --> 00:12:22.960
Hexa Knight attacks you directly!

00:12:27.790 --> 00:12:30.150
I end my turn.

00:12:45.790 --> 00:12:49.100
The key to this game is to 
successfully draw a monster.

00:12:49.780 --> 00:12:53.780
Due to the last turn, I 
know where Max Warrior is.

00:12:54.220 --> 00:12:56.940
My turn!  I summon a monster!

00:13:01.870 --> 00:13:06.160
Hexa Knight and Max Warrior 
both have 1800 attack points.

00:13:06.160 --> 00:13:11.410
However, Max Warrior gains 400 
attack points when it attacks!

00:13:12.180 --> 00:13:14.080
Go, Max Warrior!

00:13:17.060 --> 00:13:20.810
When Max Warrior destroys 
my monster in battle...

00:13:20.810 --> 00:13:25.550
...its Level, attack points and defense 
points are cut in half until your next turn.

00:13:25.870 --> 00:13:27.520
I activate a spell card!

00:13:29.170 --> 00:13:32.230
That's a trap card.  You can't activate it.

00:13:34.830 --> 00:13:39.090
But I can use it to protect 
myself from an attack next turn.

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:41.480
Next, I activate a trap!

00:13:43.460 --> 00:13:46.220
Too bad, but you can't activate that either.

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:51.980
But I've put together 
the formula for victory.

00:13:52.290 --> 00:13:57.900
I can equip Prevention Star when my 
monster switches to defense position.

00:13:58.130 --> 00:14:02.150
If I combo this with Release Restraint 
Wave that I drew before…

00:14:02.150 --> 00:14:05.000
All cards on the table are facedown.

00:14:04.980 --> 00:14:08.950
I'll be able to destroy all 
his spell and trap cards!

00:14:09.120 --> 00:14:10.530
My turn.

00:14:10.970 --> 00:14:15.370
He's doing pretty well, but no 
one can defeat me in this game.

00:14:16.210 --> 00:14:16.960
That's because...

00:14:17.940 --> 00:14:20.410
I'll also activate a spell.

00:14:20.840 --> 00:14:22.210
What?  He picked correctly again?

00:14:22.400 --> 00:14:24.990
It seems luck is still on my side.

00:14:24.980 --> 00:14:28.430
I drew the spell card Fair Exchange.

00:14:28.780 --> 00:14:32.050
I draw three cards from my deck 
and send them to the graveyard.

00:14:32.050 --> 00:14:35.610
If I send monster cards to the 
graveyard, you must discard

00:14:35.610 --> 00:14:38.080
cards from your deck equal to 
the total Level of the monsters.

00:14:38.420 --> 00:14:41.700
Which card should I choose?

00:14:42.650 --> 00:14:44.390
I choose this first.

00:14:44.650 --> 00:14:47.070
Whoa!  I already drew a good card.

00:14:47.350 --> 00:14:50.370
I drew Level 10 Decago Knight.

00:14:51.580 --> 00:14:54.070
The second will be this card.

00:14:55.310 --> 00:14:56.310
What?

00:14:56.310 --> 00:15:01.650
What luck!  I drew another 
Level 10 Decago Knight.

00:15:01.900 --> 00:15:05.680
The third will be this card.

00:15:05.680 --> 00:15:08.620
I'm excited.  If it can happen 
twice, it can happen three times.

00:15:13.030 --> 00:15:16.030
No way!  All three were Decago Knights?

00:15:16.380 --> 00:15:18.990
God gave me a miracle!

00:15:19.460 --> 00:15:21.720
The total Level is 30.

00:15:21.720 --> 00:15:25.470
Therefore, you send 30 cards 
in your deck to your graveyard.

00:15:33.610 --> 00:15:35.670
I send 30 cards to the graveyard.

00:15:36.190 --> 00:15:38.920
I activate Decago Knight's effect.

00:15:38.920 --> 00:15:43.880
When three cards with the same name are in my 
graveyard, I return them to my deck and shuffle.

00:15:46.980 --> 00:15:48.590
Then I summon a monster!

00:15:50.060 --> 00:15:51.690
I summon Triangle Knight!

00:15:53.030 --> 00:15:55.610
I end my turn.

00:15:59.300 --> 00:16:03.980
He made six moves so far, 
and he hasn't failed once.

00:16:04.840 --> 00:16:09.990
And he selected three copies of the same 
card just now.  How's that possible?

00:16:14.260 --> 00:16:15.010
Huh?

00:16:15.650 --> 00:16:22.330
The odds of drawing three copies of the same 
card are about 10,000 to 1.  Was it really random?

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:26.240
What's wrong?  You don't look so good.

00:16:26.840 --> 00:16:29.360
He's been cheating from the beginning!

00:16:29.680 --> 00:16:33.270
Max Warrior with 1800 attack 
points is on my field.

00:16:33.270 --> 00:16:36.910
Triangle Knight with 900 attack 
points is on his field.

00:16:37.220 --> 00:16:40.970
But I have no doubt that 
he has a counter ready.

00:16:41.170 --> 00:16:44.330
If I don't figure out his trick, I'll lose.

00:16:44.550 --> 00:16:47.280
What's wrong?  It's your turn.

00:16:47.850 --> 00:16:50.080
But how is he doing it?

00:16:53.880 --> 00:16:59.170
Don't worry.  When Infinity is active, 
there's a temporary blackout.

00:17:04.470 --> 00:17:05.940
It's Infinity.

00:17:09.040 --> 00:17:11.660
I found the Iliaster file!

00:17:17.320 --> 00:17:20.680
I see.  I've solved the mystery!

00:17:21.010 --> 00:17:22.510
What do you mean?

00:17:22.780 --> 00:17:25.760
My turn!  I summon a monster!

00:17:25.760 --> 00:17:28.430
I select this card!

00:17:28.430 --> 00:17:29.380
What?

00:17:30.960 --> 00:17:31.770
There it is!

00:17:31.770 --> 00:17:34.350
I summon Junk Synchron!

00:17:37.820 --> 00:17:39.830
I activate Junk Synchron's effect!

00:17:39.990 --> 00:17:42.370
When it's successfully 
summoned, I can Special

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:45.280
Summon one Level 2-or-below 
monster from my graveyard.

00:17:45.280 --> 00:17:47.440
Resurrect, Sonic Chick!

00:17:48.770 --> 00:17:53.450
What?  He used a graveyard effect 
to instantly summon two monsters!

00:17:53.900 --> 00:17:59.860
Level 3 Junk Synchron tunes Level 1 
Sonic Chick and Level 4 Max Warrior!

00:18:00.310 --> 00:18:05.020
The stars come together to form a new 
shining star!  Become the path that lights the way!

00:18:05.460 --> 00:18:06.860
Synchro Summon!

00:18:06.860 --> 00:18:09.210
Soar, Stardust Dragon!

00:18:11.180 --> 00:18:12.710
Synchro Summon!

00:18:13.170 --> 00:18:18.360
A Synchro Monster is summoned from the Extra 
Deck.  It's not affected by effects on this table.

00:18:18.680 --> 00:18:23.320
I activate the first card I drew, 
the Continuous Trap Future Battle!

00:18:23.890 --> 00:18:26.150
I select one random card in your deck.

00:18:26.150 --> 00:18:29.590
If it's a monster, it's 
Special Summoned on your

00:18:29.590 --> 00:18:33.290
field, and it's forced to battle 
against Stardust Dragon!

00:18:33.670 --> 00:18:40.160
And if Stardust Dragon destroys the monster 
in battle, I can continue to use that effect!

00:18:41.760 --> 00:18:44.490
I select that card!

00:18:50.240 --> 00:18:52.290
Go, Stardust Dragon!

00:18:52.710 --> 00:18:54.780
Shooting Sonic!

00:18:58.770 --> 00:19:00.790
The same effect activates again!

00:19:00.790 --> 00:19:03.890
I select that card!

00:19:03.890 --> 00:19:05.250
No way!

00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:08.710
It's Decago Knight.

00:19:13.970 --> 00:19:17.310
And lastly, I select that card.

00:19:18.260 --> 00:19:22.520
Flip it over.  If you 
can't, I'll do it for you.

00:19:22.960 --> 00:19:26.760
I know this card is also Decago Knight.

00:19:27.840 --> 00:19:28.710
How?

00:19:28.710 --> 00:19:31.710
Stardust Dragon!  Shooting Sonic!

00:19:36.520 --> 00:19:38.860
I lost?

00:19:38.860 --> 00:19:42.140
Cheap tricks don't work on me.

00:19:42.600 --> 00:19:45.460
Tricks?  I don't know what 
you're talking about.

00:19:45.460 --> 00:19:46.700
Then what's this?

00:19:48.590 --> 00:19:52.510
Though it was faint, I saw that your glasses 
reflected the cards during the blackout.

00:19:53.110 --> 00:19:56.770
You were using your glasses to 
determine what each card was.

00:19:57.550 --> 00:20:03.260
You memorized the cards' positions in 
that one instant and solved my trick.

00:20:04.380 --> 00:20:07.070
I lose, Yusei Fudo.

00:20:07.930 --> 00:20:09.310
How do you know my name?

00:20:11.370 --> 00:20:13.790
My company's security is perfect.

00:20:14.870 --> 00:20:18.960
Everyone who enters has their faces 
and fingerprints authenticated.

00:20:19.400 --> 00:20:22.330
I knew who you were from the beginning.

00:20:22.590 --> 00:20:25.950
I was going to punish you, 
but I underestimated you.

00:20:26.170 --> 00:20:28.210
That means you and Iliaster are-

00:20:28.210 --> 00:20:32.060
Isn't it more important to know 
whether your friends are safe?

00:20:35.320 --> 00:20:35.880
Let's go!

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:51.430
Yusei, we have the Iliaster file!

00:20:51.940 --> 00:20:52.660
There they are!

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:54.430
Hurry!  This way!

00:20:59.730 --> 00:21:01.300
Hide inside the shuttle!

00:21:05.360 --> 00:21:06.720
We're sealed in!

00:21:07.720 --> 00:21:08.760
It's a trap!

00:21:24.310 --> 00:21:28.620
Yusei Fudo, you'll vanish into 
the crevice between dimensions.

00:21:50.820 --> 00:21:56.190
Close to you  Keep what's 
precious in your heart

00:21:56.660 --> 00:22:02.900
There's only one shining 
soul that's next to you

00:22:15.880 --> 00:22:21.150
You always pretend and hide your fears

00:22:21.520 --> 00:22:26.790
You act tough and don't listen to anyone

00:22:27.090 --> 00:22:32.430
You do this over and over

00:22:32.800 --> 00:22:38.170
I shouted until my soul would break

00:22:38.440 --> 00:22:43.540
Hurry up and throw that away

00:22:44.110 --> 00:22:51.080
We're only heading towards tomorrow

00:22:51.480 --> 00:22:56.820
Close to you  If you're 
trying to find yourself

00:22:57.220 --> 00:23:02.660
Just keep doing what you ultimately decided

00:23:02.830 --> 00:23:08.130
Close to you  Keep what's 
precious in your heart

00:23:08.630 --> 00:23:16.240
There's only one shining 
soul that's next to you
